[step] Unavoidable independent seating levels: the Y475.15 port-chip backing and Y474.79 keystone inner boundary differ by 0.36 mm. Each is the finite locating/bearing plane of its purchased interface. Exact native correspondence retains those identified seats; the parallel-plane comparison does not establish an unwanted skin between them.
alternatives: A common plane requires reconciling the chip clamp stock and jack locating/retention envelope together. Moving either fitted seat merely to remove the reported level difference changes that interface.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
click: x=-48.160 y=474.790 z=307.556

[sliver] Unavoidable fitted catch projections: the 1.4 mm upper tang keeper and 1.3 mm lower latch keeper retain the purchased keystone module. Their full native profiles and actual swing/insertion clearances are identified in the receptacle review. This does not establish printed latch life or physical support cleanup.
alternatives: Filling the keeper openings enters the module envelope. Removing or sloping the working projections changes tang/latch capture; a different retention arrangement requires a complete receptacle redesign.
