[thin] Required purchased-jack swing ease: these 0.071 mm tips are where the keystone module's 50° swing ease (riteav_keystone) starts on the aperture's own top edge, which is the DATA floor plane; the ease is the path the jack swings through as it seats. Blunting the tip needs a step of at least 1.6 mm to avoid a sliver, and that step would show through the DATA opening's 1 mm margin. The tip locates nothing.
alternatives: Start the ease below the aperture edge, which puts a visible step in the DATA opening, or change the receptacle so the jack swings through another path.
