[thin] Specific board-standoff sleeve, pending Derek's decision on the main board: the main board stands 2.25 mm off the flank to clear its 2.0 mm pin tails (`wall_mounts`), on a Ø7 D sleeve with the insert in the flank behind it. The sleeve's outside is bounded by the board's 7.2 mm square wall-side keepout (pcba-tray README; J8 and J11 stand about 2 mm off the pads) and its bore must pass the Ø4.6 knurl and iron tip (Ø5, plus 0.25 at the supported crown), so its wall is 0.75-1.0 mm and at most 1.1 mm. The 1.235, 1.500 and 1.602 rows are the same sleeve meeting its 45° corbel, MH3's Ø8 footprint and the pilot's mouth. The insert's own host meets ruthex's 1.6 mm minimum in the flank. The reinforcement modifiers over these stations are infill-only (b1f86c0a2), so they draw no walls out through the flute skin.
alternatives: Revise the board's wall-side keepout round MH1-MH4 to at least 8.7 mm square (J8 and J11 move about 0.35 mm); then the standoff becomes the standard Ø8 host. A loose purchased spacer is the other route.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-back-top.step
